<%# THE WORKFLOWS SURFACE for /deployments — the five soul heartbeat launchers (Turf
    Monster / Carl / Avi / Steffon / Alex), each a copyable heartbeat prompt plus its
    acts. Titled "Workflows" because every row is a flow the operator launches, not a
    liveness signal.

    ONE FILE, TWO VARIANTS, and that is deliberate: the soul list and each soul's acts
    are decided HERE, once, and both presentations draw from that one decision.
      :summary  the Workflows summary card — ONE soul at a time on a 5-minute carousel
                (tasks/_agents_summary_card), the third card of the summary row
      :detail   the Workflows SIDEBAR — every soul and every command, stacked
                vertically, each command beside what it launches
    Two files each deciding chip membership is how a chip lands on one surface and not
    the other; test/lib/workflows_card_carve_out_test.rb reads the decision below.

    Locals:
      variant     :detail (default) or :summary
      card_class  extra card classes (optional) %>
<% variant = local_assigns.fetch(:variant, :detail) %>
<% card_class = ["rounded-xl border border-subtle bg-surface p-4", local_assigns[:card_class]].compact.join(" ") %>
<% launchers = heartbeat_launchers %>
<% souls = Agent.where(slug: launchers.map { |l| l[:agent_slug] }.uniq).index_by(&:slug) %>
<%# Card-specific visual order, plus the two acts deliberately NOT here.
    archive-shipped — production-deploy runs it as its final step, so the
    cleaning rides the release rather than waiting to be remembered.
    sleeper-auction-watch — the decision is settled in
    agents/turf_monster/HEARTBEAT.md (calendar-bound, operator-attended, so
    nothing should schedule it), and the summary card could not carry it regardless:
    the slug is 21 characters and needs 114px, while an act chip's text area on the
    carousel — two acts to a line, at its narrowest (xl, four cards) — is 98px, so it
    clips away its last ~3 characters. The longest acts that fit are 17
    (production-deploy, contest-rehearsal: 92px), so the budget is ~18. Held by
    test/system/workflows_card_chip_fit_test.rb, which FAILS if the card is ever
    widened enough to retire this reason.
    It is NOT that a chip implies a cadence — clean-infra, deploy-with-task and
    contest-rehearsal are all here, and all three are direct-invoke or
    off-sequence. That argument was retired 2026-09-09; do not restate it.
    Both acts stay invocable by name. Adding either also owes
    ACTION_DESCRIPTIONS + ACTION_ICONS keys and the arrays pinned in
    application_helper_test.rb, and test/lib/workflows_card_carve_out_test.rb
    holds THIS comment to the helper's "deliberately ABSENT" list, so a third
    carve-out cannot land here in silence. %>
<% entries = launchers.map do |launcher|
     card_actions = case launcher[:agent_slug]
                    when "carl" then ["pr-review", "pr-review-slow"]
                    when "avi" then ["qa-release", "deploy-with-task"]
                    when "steffon" then ["production-deploy", "clean-infra", "workspace-launch"]
                    else launcher[:actions]
                    end
     { launcher: launcher, soul: souls[launcher[:agent_slug]], actions: card_actions }
   end %>
<% if variant == :summary %>
  <%# THE CAROUSEL STARTS ON TURF MONSTER — the operator's spec — and walks the rest in
      their canonical order, wrapping, so it reads as a circle rather than a list. %>
  <% first = entries.index { |entry| entry[:launcher][:agent_slug] == "turf-monster" } || 0 %>
  <%= render "tasks/agents_summary_card", entries: entries.rotate(first) %>
<% else %>
  <%= render "components/copy_text_script" %>
  <div id="heartbeats-card"
       class="<%= card_class %>"
       data-test="heartbeats-card">
    <p class="text-[11px] text-muted">Copy any phrase to launch that soul's workflow.</p>
    <%# ONE SOUL PER ROW, vertically — the sidebar's width is what lets every command
        sit beside its description, which the half-width card of five columns never
        could. No compact toggle: nothing here is hidden. %>
    <div class="mt-4 flex flex-col divide-y divide-subtle/70" data-test="heartbeats-list">
      <% entries.each do |entry| %>
        <div class="py-3 first:pt-0 last:pb-0">
          <%= render "tasks/heartbeat_launcher", launcher: entry[:launcher], soul: entry[:soul],
                     actions: entry[:actions], layout: :row %>
        </div>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% end %>
